OL,3,  V-,,%-,,%-,,%S#"!##!###!##!
OL,5, Talks between Ford management and
OL,6, unions broke down after the unions
OL,7, rejected an improved pay offer.
OL,9,FUnions' leader Mick Murphy said an
OL,10,Fall-out strike by 32,500 Ford manual
OL,11,Fworkers would start on Monday unless
OL,12,Fthe company requested more talks.
OL,14,FThe company said it had made "a number
OL,15,Fof proposals" at a six-hour meeting but
OL,16,Fdid not give details.
OL,17,F
OL,18,FIts earlier offer of a three-year
OL,19,Fpackage was rejected by 88 per cent of
OL,20,Fthe workforce.
OL,23,T]CFrom 28-01-88 / teletextarchive.com
OL,24,ANext PageBT'text FilesCRewindFReg Radio
